1764	8c8c6003-d548-453c-ae24-30d39c3ea587	agent_completed	negative_rep	customer	1	Testimony completed	{"agent_id": "negative_rep", "round_number": 1, "status": "completed", "started_at": "2026-05-15T15:34:10.431037", "completed_at": "2026-05-15T15:34:21.972551", "raw_response": "```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent_id\\": \\"negative_rep\\",\\n  \\"agent_name\\": \\"David Okonkwo\\",\\n  \\"role\\": \\"VP of Engineering \\u2014 Platform Infrastructure\\",\\n  \\"experience_type\\": \\"negative\\",\\n  \\"round\\": 1,\\n  \\"experience_summary\\": \\"My experience with these cloud vendors has been largely defined by operational failures and support shortcomings that directly impacted Meridian Logistics' ability to meet critical SLAs. The promises made during sales cycles rarely translated into reliable production environments, leading to significant team frustration and costly downtime.\\",\\n  \\"vendor_experiences\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": {\\n      \\"overall\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"worked\\": [],\\n      \\"failed\\": [],\\n      \\"trust\\": 0.0\\n    },\\n    \\"Azure\\": {\\n      \\"overall\\": \\"Our experience with Azure was plagued by unexpected complexity and support delays that cost us valuable time and revenue. The initial promise of seamless integration with SAP S/4HANA was a mirage, and their compliance posture for EU data sovereignty was questionable, leading to significant operational friction.\\",\\n      \\"worked\\": [\\n        \\"Azure Active Directory integration via SAML 2.0/OIDC was functional for basic access control.\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\"failed\\": [\\n        \\"The Frankfurt and Dublin multi-region deployment suffered from inconsistent latency, exceeding the sub-20ms requirement between cloud instances and our Frankfurt data center during peak loads.\\",\\n        \\"Auto-scaling for peak traffic spikes failed to reliably handle 300% increases, resulting in service degradation and lost transactions during critical seasonal logistics periods.\\",\\n        \\"The migration of 450+ VMs and 12TB of PostgreSQL/SAP HANA data took 20 weeks, 4 weeks longer than projected, due to unforeseen compatibility issues with their managed PostgreSQL service.\\",\\n        \\"The promised 99.99% uptime SLA was breached twice in Q3 due to unannounced network maintenance in the Dublin region, impacting our core production workloads for over 4 hours each time.\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\"trust\\": 0.3\\n    },\\n    \\"GCP\\": {\\n      \\"overall\\": \\"GCP's Kubernetes offering, while feature-rich on paper, proved immature in practice, leading to stability issues and significant engineering effort to maintain. Their support for critical incidents was slow, and the lack of specific German compliance certifications made them a non-starter for Meridian Logistics.\\",\\n      \\"worked\\": [\\n        \\"Basic Kubernetes cluster provisioning was straightforward.\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\"failed\\": [\\n        \\"The OmegaKube platform, while feature-rich, was unstable under production load. We experienced frequent pod evictions and cluster reboots, directly impacting our microservices deployments.\\",\\n        \\"The AI-assisted right-sizing tool, which promised a 28% compute bill reduction, was overly aggressive and led to performance degradation on critical SAP HANA workloads, requiring manual intervention and costly over-provisioning.\\",\\n        \\"During a P1 incident involving a database cluster failure on January 15th, the response time from GCP support was over 45 minutes, far exceeding the 15-minute SLA, resulting in a 3-hour outage for our order processing system.\\",\\n        \\"The GDPR DPA being governed by Singapore law and the inherent CLOUD Act exposure presented an unacceptable attack surface for Meridian Logistics, making them non-compliant with EU data sovereignty requirements.\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\"trust\\": 0.2\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"what_worked\\": [\\n    \\"Azure Active Directory integration via SAML 2.0/OIDC was functional for basic access control.\\",\\n    \\"Basic Kubernetes cluster provisioning on GCP was straightforward.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"what_failed\\": [\\n    \\"Azure's multi-region deployment suffered from inconsistent latency, exceeding the sub-20ms requirement between cloud instances and our Frankfurt data center during peak loads.\\",\\n    \\"Azure's auto-scaling for peak traffic spikes failed to reliably handle 300% increases, resulting in service degradation and lost transactions during critical seasonal logistics periods.\\",\\n    \\"The migration of 450+ VMs and 12TB of PostgreSQL/SAP HANA data to Azure took 20 weeks, 4 weeks longer than projected, due to unforeseen compatibility issues with their managed PostgreSQL service.\\",\\n    \\"Azure's promised 99.99% uptime SLA was breached twice in Q3 due to unannounced network maintenance in the Dublin region, impacting our core production workloads for over 4 hours each time.\\",\\n    \\"GCP's OmegaKube platform was unstable under production load, leading to frequent pod evictions and cluster reboots, directly impacting our microservices deployments.\\",\\n    \\"GCP's AI-assisted right-sizing tool was overly aggressive and led to performance degradation on critical SAP HANA workloads, requiring manual intervention and costly over-provisioning.\\",\\n    \\"During a P1 incident involving a database cluster failure on January 15th, the response time from GCP support was over 45 minutes, far exceeding the 15-minute SLA, resulting in a 3-hour outage for our order processing system.\\",\\n    \\"GCP's GDPR DPA being governed by Singapore law and the inherent CLOUD Act exposure presented an unacceptable attack surface for Meridian Logistics, making them non-compliant with EU data sovereignty requirements.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"operational_pain_points\\": [\\n    \\"The inconsistency in Azure's network latency between regions directly impacted our real-time logistics tracking applications, causing delays and customer dissatisfaction.\\",\\n    \\"The failure of Azure's auto-scaling during peak seasons meant our teams spent countless hours manually scaling resources, diverting them from proactive development and innovation.\\",\\n    \\"The extended migration timeline for Azure cost Meridian Logistics an estimated \\u20ac1.5 million in delayed project benefits and additional internal resource allocation.\\",\\n    \\"Azure's SLA breaches led to direct financial penalties and a significant erosion of trust with our operational teams who depend on system stability.\\",\\n    \\"The instability of GCP's Kubernetes platform required constant firefighting from our engineering teams, consuming roughly 30% of their capacity and preventing them from delivering on new feature roadmaps.\\",\\n    \\"The aggressive nature of GCP's cost optimization tools forced us to revert to manual capacity planning, negating the promised operational overhead reduction.\\",\\n    \\"The slow response from GCP support during critical incidents meant our teams were left to diagnose and mitigate issues themselves, often with incomplete information, prolonging downtime.\\",\\n    \\"The legal and compliance risks associated with GCP's data processing agreements created a constant state of anxiety and required extensive legal review, slowing down our adoption.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"support_reality\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": {\\n      \\"actual_response\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"quality\\": \\"Not experienced\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"Azure\\": {\\n      \\"actual_response\\": \\"P1 incident response averaged 40 minutes, with some critical issues taking over an hour to even acknowledge. Non-urgent queries to our dedicated TAM often took 6-8 hours for a response, if at all.\\",\\n      \\"quality\\": \\"The support team was often reactive and lacked deep understanding of our specific SAP S/4HANA integration challenges. TAM continuity was an issue, with replacements taking weeks to onboard, further delaying resolution.\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"GCP\\": {\\n      \\"actual_response\\": \\"P1 incident response averaged 45 minutes, with critical outages taking significantly longer to get initial engagement. Our dedicated TAM was rarely available for immediate assistance, and response times for non-critical issues were typically 12-24 hours.\\",\\n      \\"quality\\": \\"The support team seemed overwhelmed and lacked the specialized knowledge required for our complex Kubernetes and SAP HANA environments. The lack of proactive engagement meant we often had to escalate multiple times to get adequate attention.\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"onboarding_reality\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": {\\n      \\"actual_timeline\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"blockers\\": []\\n    },\\n    \\"Azure\\": {\\n      \\"actual_timeline\\": \\"20 weeks (4 weeks longer than projected)\\",\\n      \\"blockers\\": [\\n        \\"Unforeseen complexities in configuring private connectivity to meet latency requirements.\\",\\n        \\"Compatibility issues with migrating specific PostgreSQL versions to their managed service.\\",\\n        \\"Lack of clear documentation on integrating with SAP S/4HANA in a multi-region EU setup.\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \\"GCP\\": {\\n      \\"actual_timeline\\": \\"18 weeks (3 weeks longer than projected)\\",\\n      \\"blockers\\": [\\n        \\"The immaturity of their Kubernetes platform required extensive custom configuration and troubleshooting.\\",\\n        \\"Difficulty in achieving the required sub-20ms latency between Frankfurt and Dublin regions for our critical logistics data streams.\\",\\n        \\"The lack of readily available SAP HANA performance tuning guides for their OmegaCompute X4 instances.\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"edge_case_failures\\": [\\n    \\"During a severe weather event in Q4, Azure's disaster recovery mechanisms failed to meet the RTO of <2 hours for our primary logistics management system, leading to an extended 4-hour downtime.\\",\\n    \\"On GCP, a rare confluence of events involving a Kubernetes node failure and a subsequent automated scaling event caused a cascading failure that took 6 hours to fully resolve, impacting our financial reporting systems.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"risk_signals\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"Azure\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"Inconsistent latency and auto-scaling failures during peak traffic, directly impacting Meridian Logistics' ability to meet customer delivery promises.\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Lost revenue, customer churn, and increased operational costs due to manual intervention.\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"GCP\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"Kubernetes platform immaturity and instability, leading to frequent outages and significant engineering overhead for Meridian Logistics.\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Delayed product development, increased engineering costs, and reputational damage due to unreliable services.\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"GCP\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"GDPR DPA governed by Singapore law and CLOUD Act exposure, creating a critical legal and compliance attack surface for Meridian Logistics.\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Risk of regulatory fines, legal challenges, and inability to operate within EU data sovereignty mandates.\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"trust_per_vendor\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": 0.0,\\n    \\"Azure\\": 0.3,\\n    \\"GCP\\": 0.2\\n  },\\n  \\"decision_impact\\": \\"Based on my direct experience, the decision to commit to any of these vendors for Meridian Logistics' mission-critical systems is fraught with risk. The operational failures, support deficiencies, and compliance gaps observed mean that a significant investment would be required to mitigate these issues, potentially outweighing any perceived benefits.\\",\\n  \\"confidence\\": 0.8\\n}\\n```", "parsed_output": {"agent_id": "negative_rep", "agent_name": "David Okonkwo", "role": "VP of Engin