1827	8c8c6003-d548-453c-ae24-30d39c3ea587	agent_completed	positive_rep	customer	1	Testimony completed	{"agent_id": "positive_rep", "round_number": 1, "status": "completed", "started_at": "2026-05-15T15:34:10.447019", "completed_at": "2026-05-15T15:34:22.148804", "raw_response": "{\\n  \\"agent_id\\": \\"positive_rep\\",\\n  \\"agent_name\\": \\"Rachel Park\\",\\n  \\"role\\": \\"Senior IT Director \\u2014 Cloud Migrations\\",\\n  \\"experience_type\\": \\"positive\\",\\n  \\"round\\": 1,\\n  \\"experience_summary\\": \\"My team and I have had a largely positive experience with CloudPrime, particularly for our SAP workloads and EU data requirements. While onboarding had some initial density, production usage has been stable, and support has been responsive when needed. NexaCloud showed promise with its AI capabilities, but the TISAX gap was a significant concern for Meridian Logistics.\\",\\n  \\"vendor_experiences\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": {\\n      \\"overall\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"worked\\": [],\\n      \\"failed\\": [],\\n      \\"trust\\": 0.0\\n    },\\n    \\"Azure\\": {\\n      \\"overall\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"worked\\": [],\\n      \\"failed\\": [],\\n      \\"trust\\": 0.0\\n    },\\n    \\"GCP\\": {\\n      \\"overall\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"worked\\": [],\\n      \\"failed\\": [],\\n      \\"trust\\": 0.0\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"what_worked\\": [\\n    \\"CloudPrime's robust SAP S/4HANA integration and performance in our Frankfurt region deployment met our sub-20ms latency requirements. The high availability for core production workloads consistently exceeded 99.99% uptime.\\",\\n    \\"NexaCloud's CostIntelligence tool was surprisingly effective for optimizing spend even on non-ML workloads, providing clear visibility into our cloud expenditure.\\",\\n    \\"DataVault's LogiStack platform connectors significantly reduced integration development time for our existing systems, a real win for our development teams.\\",\\n    \\"SkyBridge's SkyBridge Connect provided a seamless hybrid integration, which was critical for our initial migration phase, allowing our on-premise systems to communicate effectively with the cloud environment.\\",\\n    \\"OmegaCloud's OmegaCompute X4 performance was indeed top-tier during our testing, and the AI-assisted right-sizing feature did deliver a noticeable reduction in compute costs, around 28% in our pilot.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"what_failed\\": [\\n    \\"OmegaCloud's GDPR DPA being governed by Singapore law presented a critical compliance red flag for Meridian Logistics, making it a non-starter for our EU data sovereignty needs. The CLOUD Act exposure was also a major concern.\\",\\n    \\"SkyBridge had a significant TISAX gap that directly led to them losing the Volkswagen contract, a clear indicator of their inability to meet critical automotive client requirements, which is a risk for us.\\",\\n    \\"DataVault's Kubernetes platform is clearly a generation 1 offering. We experienced limitations when trying to deploy more complex microservices, requiring manual workarounds that slowed down our innovation pipeline.\\",\\n    \\"NexaCloud's Frankfurt second availability zone was not available for the first six months of our evaluation period, directly impacting our high availability requirements for critical production workloads in the EU.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"operational_pain_points\\": [\\n    \\"For CloudPrime, while P1 incidents were handled well, the dedicated TAM sometimes took 4-6 hours for non-urgent queries. This meant my team had to wait for critical but not immediate configuration advice, impacting day-to-day workflow efficiency.\\",\\n    \\"The initial onboarding documentation for CloudPrime was quite dense. It took my team three full days of dedicated effort just to understand the network configuration options, which delayed our initial deployment timeline by a few days.\\",\\n    \\"DataVault experienced capacity constraints during Q4 peak traffic. We had to manually allocate resources, which was time-consuming and detracted from our focus on strategic initiatives.\\",\\n    \\"SkyBridge's standard support P1 SLA of 1 hour was simply too long for our mission-critical systems. We had a minor incident where a service was down for 45 minutes before initial acknowledgement, which would have been unacceptable in production.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"support_reality\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": {\\n      \\"actual_response\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"quality\\": \\"Not experienced\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"Azure\\": {\\n      \\"actual_response\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"quality\\": \\"Not experienced\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"GCP\\": {\\n      \\"actual_response\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"quality\\": \\"Not experienced\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"onboarding_reality\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": {\\n      \\"actual_timeline\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"blockers\\": []\\n    },\\n    \\"Azure\\": {\\n      \\"actual_timeline\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"blockers\\": []\\n    },\\n    \\"GCP\\": {\\n      \\"actual_timeline\\": \\"Not experienced\\",\\n      \\"blockers\\": []\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"edge_case_failures\\": [\\n    \\"During a peak logistics spike for Meridian Logistics, DataVault's Kubernetes platform struggled to auto-scale effectively for our new microservices, requiring manual intervention and causing a temporary performance degradation.\\",\\n    \\"We encountered an issue with OmegaCloud where a support ticket's data was being processed in Singapore, which raised concerns given our strict EU data residency requirements, even though the initial P1 response was within SLA.\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"risk_signals\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"OmegaCloud\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"GDPR DPA governed by Singapore law and CLOUD Act exposure\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Significant risk to data sovereignty and legal compliance for Meridian Logistics, making them non-compliant with EU regulations.\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"SkyBridge\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"TISAX and BSI C5 gaps\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Directly led to lost business with Volkswagen, indicating a failure to meet critical certification requirements for clients in regulated industries like automotive.\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"DataVault\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"Kubernetes platform being generation 1 and less mature\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Poses a significant risk for organizations relying heavily on containerization and microservices, potentially leading to performance issues and increased development friction.\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"vendor\\": \\"NexaCloud\\",\\n      \\"risk\\": \\"Frankfurt second availability zone not available during the first 6 months\\",\\n      \\"operational_impact\\": \\"Directly impacts high availability requirements for production workloads in the EU, creating a critical gap for Meridian Logistics.\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"trust_per_vendor\\": {\\n    \\"AWS\\": 0.0,\\n    \\"Azure\\": 0.0,\\n    \\"GCP\\": 0.0\\n  },\\n  \\"decision_impact\\": \\"Based on my team's lived experience, CloudPrime stands out as the most reliable and compliant option for Meridian Logistics, especially given our need for EU data sovereignty and strong SAP integration. While other vendors had individual strengths, their critical gaps in compliance or platform maturity presented unacceptable risks.\\",\\n  \\"confidence\\": 0.9\\n}", "parsed_output": {"agent_id": "positive_rep", "agent_name": "Rachel Park", "role": "Senior IT Director \\u2014 Cloud Migrations", "experience_type": "positive", "round": 1, "experience_summary": "My team and I have had a largely positive experience with CloudPrime, particularly for our SAP workloads and EU data requirements. While onboarding had some initial density, production usage has been stable, and support has been responsive when needed. NexaCl